 1. Build Failure Scenario
Q: "Your Maven build suddenly fails with a Missing artifact error. How would you troubleshoot?"
👉 Expected Approach:
Check pom.xml for correct version and groupId/artifactId
Ensure the artifact exists in the configured repository (Maven Central/Nexus/Artifactory)
Clear .m2/repository cache and re-download
Validate proxy and internet settings
🏗️ 2. Managing Multi-Module Builds
Q: "You’re working on a multi-module Maven project, and one module fails during build. What steps would you take?"
👉 Look For:
Use mvn clean install -pl <module-name> -am to build only affected module and dependencies
Check for interdependencies and proper module hierarchy in parent pom.xml
Validate plugin versions or snapshot dependencies
📦 3. Dependency Conflict
Q: "Your Maven project compiles but behaves incorrectly due to different versions of the same dependency being used. How do you resolve it?"
👉 Response:
Use mvn dependency:tree to identify version conflicts
Apply dependency exclusion in pom.xml
Use dependency management section in parent POM to enforce consistent versions
🔄 4. Integration with Jenkins
Q: "Your Jenkins pipeline fails during the Maven test phase. What do you investigate first?"
👉 Good Answers:
Validate Maven is correctly installed/configured on the Jenkins node
Check settings.xml or .m2 repo if dependencies are not being downloaded
Review logs for test failures, missing env variables, or plugin issues
🧩 5. Custom Plugin Issue
Q: "You wrote a Maven plugin or goal, but it's not being executed. How would you debug?"
👉 Solution Steps:
Ensure plugin is defined under build > plugins in pom.xml
Verify correct lifecycle phase is mapped
Use mvn help:effective-pom to verify plugin visibility
Check logs with -X for debug-level info
🗃️ 6. Artifact Not Uploaded to Nexus/Artifactory
Q: "The Maven deploy phase doesn't push artifacts to Nexus. What could be the issue?"
👉 Possible Causes:
Incorrect distributionManagement URL
Wrong credentials in settings.xml
Missing maven-deploy-plugin
Proxy or SSL handshake failure
⚙️ 7. Need to Speed Up Builds
Q: "Your Maven build takes too long. What optimizations can you suggest?"
👉 Suggestions:
Use parallel builds: mvn -T 1C install
Use incremental builds
Cache dependencies with CI tools (e.g., .m2 directory in Jenkins)
Avoid unnecessary plugins
👨💻 8. Need to Add a Local JAR
Q: "Your team wants to use a JAR not available in Maven Central. How do you include it?"
👉 You can:
Use mvn install:install-file to add the JAR to the local repository
Or deploy it to Nexus/Artifactory and reference via pom.xml
